    a: "This module covers two kinds of deals. In M&A, a sell-side team runs a company's sale, usually as an auction, and buy-side teams help bidders win at the right price. Bids start non-binding and firm up until a purchase agreement is signed; closing follows once approvals such as antitrust clearance arrive. The agreement allocates risk through reps, indemnities, conditions and price adjustments. In equity capital markets (ECM), banks underwrite IPOs, follow-on share sales and convertible bonds, pricing each off investor demand.",
